                        ],
                        "form": "гро́гах"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "6066ae99-ea66-4cbd-bb9a-9c179a99d314",
                        "entry_id": "5bdbc379-7e2f-3187-b845-a9e2ddd7416a",
                        "tags": [
                            "singular"
                        ],
                        "form": "гро́гу"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b2dd64da-23d5-3ca2-81e2-ddafbe770b1c",
                        "entry_id": "5bdbc379-7e2f-3187-b845-a9e2ddd7416a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "крепкий спиртной напиток, приготовленный из водки или рома, разбавленного горячей водой с сахаром"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f03bbf4b-875d-4728-95a8-dc3299b80240",
                                "sense_id": "b2dd64da-23d5-3ca2-81e2-ddafbe770b1c",
                                "text": "В награду пьяным ― он нальёт // И пунш, и грог душистый .."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7cfb2ad3-1af8-446b-b436-cb0fb11ed9bc",
                                "sense_id": "b2dd64da-23d5-3ca2-81e2-ddafbe770b1c",
                                "text": "Послужи с моё да испытай столько же бурь, тогда уверишься, что добрый стакан грогу лучше всех непромокаемых шинелей и всех противопростудных лекарств .."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ef50906c-be92-4359-80c1-9ae775868037",
                                "sense_id": "b2dd64da-23d5-3ca2-81e2-ddafbe770b1c",
                                "text": "Я спросил стакан грогу, усаживаясь в стойло под трельяжем."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f06ea0b2-0772-4e4b-82fe-f7a5c96800f4",
                        "source_entry_id": "5bdbc379-7e2f-3187-b845-a9e2ddd7416a",
                        "source_sense_id": "b2dd64da-23d5-3ca2-81e2-ddafbe770b1c",
                        "target_lang_word": "grog",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "grog",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "190c5607-0c80-3025-84e5-c80ab2377cbe",
                                        "entry_id": "d7eb30f5-3e58-3e89-82ce-29614785e328",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An alcoholic beverage made with rum and water, especially that once issued to sailors of the Royal Navy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b0e11470-7937-4655-bac6-cb3cb6548b2f",
                                                "sense_id": "190c5607-0c80-3025-84e5-c80ab2377cbe",
                                                "text": "[…] giving him a calebash, and the best part of a bottle of my rum, I desired him to run to the creek, and make me some grog, and this he did; but the poor fellow, never having made grog before, poured in all the spirits and but very little water, doubtless thinking, that the stronger it was the better; which beverage I swallowed to the bottom, without taking time to taste it, and I became instantly so much intoxicated that I could hardly keep my feet."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3084af69-feef-3d2a-a597-4292e21c4353",
                                        "entry_id": "d7eb30f5-3e58-3e89-82ce-29614785e328",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An alcoholic beverage made with rum and water, especially that once issued to sailors of the Royal Navy.",
                                            "An alcoholic beverage made with hot water or tea, sugar and rum, sometimes also with lemon or lime juice and spices, particularly cinnamon."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e27362aa-ebd4-3a8b-9515-3439e6548698",
                                        "entry_id": "d7eb30f5-3e58-3e89-82ce-29614785e328",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any alcoholic beverage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Australia",
                                            "New-Zealand",
                                            "broadly",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db6b729a-aff0-426f-a0f1-745c6a920058",
                                                "sense_id": "e27362aa-ebd4-3a8b-9515-3439e6548698",
                                                "text": "I quite understood their drift, and after a stiff glass of grog, or rather more of the same, and with each a sovereign in hand, they made light of the attack, and swore they would encounter a worse madman any day for the pleasure of meeting so 'bloomin' good a bloke' as your correspondent."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ecf2ed66-258c-37cb-b803-bd02d24df175",
                                        "entry_id": "d7eb30f5-3e58-3e89-82ce-29614785e328",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A glass or serving of an alcoholic beverage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Australia",
                                            "New-Zealand",
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a547d93c-2f19-46c5-87e3-21e6dbc73fba",
                                                "sense_id": "ecf2ed66-258c-37cb-b803-bd02d24df175",
                                                "text": "1950, Nevil Shute, A Town Like Alice [The Legacy], New York: William Morrow, Chapter 5, p. 138,\nJoe […] told them how he had been nailed up to be beaten, and they shouted another grog for him."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f1f43e38-14df-369b-8c9e-4a208d80346b",
                                        "entry_id": "d7eb30f5-3e58-3e89-82ce-29614785e328",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A type of pre-fired clay that has been ground and screened to a specific particle size."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "grog",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1529290d-0442-339b-9350-7a02abb8419b",
                                        "entry_id": "73dbde02-e3c5-3167-83d7-c2609b54adf0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To grind and screen (clay) to a specific particle size."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "31b42140-4dd7-3547-bc33-3d4ee51faeaf",
                                        "entry_id": "73dbde02-e3c5-3167-83d7-c2609b54adf0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To drink alcohol."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b5bd0c9-eac6-4bd4-9e7b-7056b0a4cc56",
                                                "sense_id": "31b42140-4dd7-3547-bc33-3d4ee51faeaf",
                                                "text": "[…] a practice of “equal surrender.” This evocative phrase comes from Basil Sansom's ethnography […] of grogging sessions among Aboriginal communities in Darwin. Sansom argues that this style of communal drinking […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a1fa091a-ab64-49fb-a168-ce8f938bc72d",
                        "source_entry_id": "5bdbc379-7e2f-3187-b845-a9e2ddd7416a",
                        "source_sense_id": "b2dd64da-23d5-3ca2-81e2-ddafbe770b1c",
                        "target_lang_word": "Grog",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Grog",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8351e63f-cfbb-3af6-b525-e110d060d31b",
                                        "entry_id": "2cec4138-e960-3f3b-a0aa-df2ab2d813d9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "heißes Getränk aus Rum (auch Weinbrand oder Arrak) mit Wasser und Zucker"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "054d2767-d370-4eb2-b317-1dae97b44275",
                                                "sense_id": "8351e63f-cfbb-3af6-b525-e110d060d31b",
                                                "text": "„Aus der Leutnantskabine kam der Duft von Grog.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3de935ef-0372-4879-836f-0fdf2de3d041",
                                                "sense_id": "8351e63f-cfbb-3af6-b525-e110d060d31b",
                                                "text": "„Ich war vollauf damit beschäftigt, Ben mit einem steifen Grog wieder auf die Beine zu bringen und Mrs. Hawkins ein Beruhigungsmittel zu verabfolgen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f2f26e3d-6f96-419b-96f8-47a12b88bdad",
                                                "sense_id": "8351e63f-cfbb-3af6-b525-e110d060d31b",
                                                "text": "„Eine Weile hatte ich sehr ernste und abgeklärte Gedanken, doch meine neuen Schiffskameraden, von denen einige tatsächlich alte Kameraden von anderen Seglern waren, konnten mich mit Grog aufmuntern.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0fff8de5-d2b4-442c-a936-b7d417537e92",
                        "source_entry_id": "5bdbc379-7e2f-3187-b845-a9e2ddd7416a",
                        "source_sense_id": "b2dd64da-23d5-3ca2-81e2-ddafbe770b1c",
                        "target_lang_word": "grog",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "grog",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "95291cb2-e94e-3161-993d-006743b1eab3",
                                        "entry_id": "ccf2f37a-bde4-387e-a5cc-5e6d4d101578",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Boisson chaude à base d’eau et de rhum."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "66383af3-2dda-4acc-90f1-4593c7373d3a",
                                                "sense_id": "95291cb2-e94e-3161-993d-006743b1eab3",
                                                "text": "Les grogs brûlants ne furent pas épargnés, et le brave sergent Long put en prendre sa part."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "903212f0-743a-4dac-b713-e3782f89da7c",
                                                "sense_id": "95291cb2-e94e-3161-993d-006743b1eab3",
                                                "text": "elle posa ... un plateau devant Clémence, qui se mit à préparer posément son grog, versant l’eau chaude sur le citron, qu’elle écrasait à coups de cuiller, sucrant, mettant le rhum en consultant le carafon, pour ne pas dépasser le petit verre réglementaire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2073cd2d-1273-4ad5-a503-3f30483d46b3",
                                                "sense_id": "95291cb2-e94e-3161-993d-006743b1eab3",
                                                "text": "– Ça ne te ferait rien de prendre un grog au mois de juin ? C’est une bonne boisson de vaincu, en toutes saisons."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c32ad67a-c3b0-451f-b606-65c1d56da2eb",
                                                "sense_id": "95291cb2-e94e-3161-993d-006743b1eab3",
                                                "text": "Tout en parlant, mon compagnon s’était approché du comptoir, où je le rejoignis, et l’on nous servit nos grogs."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
